  [FAIL] lev-2 THE DECIDING CHECK against candidate K4, written so it can exonerate it: k04's 1 + 2/ln(1/f) must agree with the true lever of item 16's estimator to 20%.  IT DOES NOT -- it has the OPPOSITE SIGN and is 1.7x to 2.9x too large in magnitude.  K4's headline identity is REFUTED.   (f_DM=0.9: true -1.109 vs k04 +1.869;  f_DM=0.5: true -1.885 vs k04 +3.885;  f_DM=0.1: true -6.817 vs k04 +19.982)
  [PASS] lev-3 DIAGNOSIS, and it exonerates k04's arithmetic while condemning its transcription: 1 + 2/ln(1/f) is the EXACT derivative of a0 = (1-f_DM) g_obs / [ln(1/(1-f_DM))]^2 -- the baryonic share substituted into the logarithm where the DARK share belongs.  k04's finite-difference check passed because it differentiated the same wrong function.   (k04's own estimator has lever +3.8854 at f_DM=0.5, and its formula gives +3.8854: exact.  Item 16's estimator has -1.8854.)
  [PASS] lev-4 the two estimators are not two writings of one thing -- they return different a_0 from the same measurement, so this is a transcription error and not a convention.  (They coincide at exactly one point, f_DM = 1/2, where the baryonic and dark shares are equal and the substitution is invisible -- which is precisely why an eyeball check would not have caught it.)   (at f_DM = 0.30, g_obs = 1e-10: item 16 gives 4.8291e-11, k04's gives 5.5024e-10 (+1039%);  at f_DM = 0.50 they agree exactly (1.0407e-10))
  [PASS] lev-5 MUTATION CONTROL: the lever is a property of the KERNEL, so swapping Route A for the 'simple' kernel must move it materially.  If it did not, the identity would be arithmetic rather than physics and would not test the framework at all.   (at f_DM = 0.5 Route A gives -1.885, 'simple' gives -2.000; at f_DM = 0.1 -6.817 vs -10.000 (max deviation 47%))
  [PASS] lev-5b the two analytic limits of the TRUE lever, which are checkable by hand: deep MOND (f_DM -> 1) must give exactly -1, because there a_0 = g_obs^2/g_bar; deep Newton (f_DM -> 0) must DIVERGE, because a baryon-dominated system carries no information about a_0.  The LambdaCDM/Newtonian alternative is therefore not a rival number but 'N/A by construction' -- with no acceleration scale there is nothing to invert for.   (f_DM -> 1: Lambda = -1.000000;  f_DM -> 0: Lambda = -9.651e+07)
  [PASS] lev-6 BOTH FOOTINGS: the lever contains neither a_0 nor g_obs, so it is bit-identical on the canonical and alt footings.  Verified rather than asserted.   (canonical a0 = 9.360e-11 and alt a0 = 1.130e-10 both give Lambda(f_DM=0.30) = -2.876057)

